              { "type": "Paragraph", "set_style": { "style_names": ["iq-breakdown-copy"] }, "set_text": { "text": "Every ink color in your design requires its own physical screen setup before a single shirt hits the press. More colors mean more screens, more labor, and more setup time. Keeping your palette tight—especially on smaller runs—is one of the fastest ways to protect your per-unit cost." } }
